# RustLace — ignore rules
#
# The repository ships no build output, no local scratch state and no secrets.
# Everything below is either regenerable or machine-local; if a file here ever
# needs to be committed deliberately, use `git add -f <path>` and say why in the
# commit. AGENTS.md records the same rule: never commit build outputs, `%APPDATA%`
# state, certificates, `.pfx` files, private keys or secrets.

# --- Rust build output -------------------------------------------------------
# Workspace target directory, plus the standalone UI spike, which is deliberately
# outside the workspace and therefore has its own.
/target/
/lovelace-desktop-spike/target/

# --- Local scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
# `--journey ... --out .tmp\journey` and other acceptance modes write here.
/.tmp/

# --- Local working artifacts ------------------------------------------------
# Agentic and release-check runs leave these beside the tree. They are useful
# while working and never part of the repository content.
/.round3-artifact/
/.round4/
/linux-job-*.log
/pr-body.md

# --- Secrets and certificates ------------------------------------------------
# A release is unsigned by default; a signing key is never committed.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
/.secrets/

# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
/.idea/
/.vscode/

# --- Python caches -----------------------------------------------------------
# `python tools/check-architecture.py` and the other tools write bytecode beside
# the scripts; it is regenerable and never part of the repository content.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Kept deliberately: `Cargo.lock` (a binary workspace pins its graph),
# `docs/goal-desktop-v4/` capture references, and `.dsh/skills/`.
